WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.540
As environments grow more complex, detection engineering becomes increasingly important.

00:00:04.540 --> 00:00:09.000
Organizations need maintainable detections, reliable telemetry, strong documentation,

00:00:09.000 --> 00:00:11.000
meaningful metrics, and effective collaboration.

00:00:11.000 --> 00:00:16.000
Cloud services, SaaS platforms, identity systems, endpoint tooling, applications,

00:00:16.000 --> 00:00:17.965
and data pipelines all change quickly.

00:00:17.965 --> 00:00:21.970
Detection programs must adapt without losing control of quality or ownership.

00:00:21.970 --> 00:00:25.635
The future of detection engineering is not just more alerts or more tools.

00:00:25.635 --> 00:00:29.155
It is better visibility, clearer context, stronger lifecycle management,

00:00:29.155 --> 00:00:32.370
and more disciplined improvement based on operational evidence.

00:00:32.370 --> 00:00:36.490
Automation and AI can help with parts of the work, such as summarization, enrichment,

00:00:36.490 --> 00:00:38.100
review support, or test generation.

00:00:38.100 --> 00:00:42.300
Human judgment remains essential for understanding business context, investigation needs,

00:00:42.300 --> 00:00:44.023
and acceptable operational tradeoffs.

00:00:44.023 --> 00:00:47.905
Detection engineering helps create sustainable defensive capabilities that evolve

00:00:47.905 --> 00:00:50.000
alongside changing threats,

00:00:50.000 --> 00:00:51.760
technologies, and business requirements.

00:00:51.760 --> 00:00:55.875
The organizations that benefit most will treat detection as a long-term engineering

00:00:55.875 --> 00:00:56.325
practice.

00:00:56.325 --> 00:00:59.950
Future programs will likely place more emphasis on detection portability,

00:00:59.950 --> 00:01:03.160
structured metadata, testable detection content, coverage mapping,

00:01:03.160 --> 00:01:06.520
and tighter connections between detection work and incident response lessons.

00:01:06.520 --> 00:01:10.632
They will also need stronger partnerships with data engineering and platform teams.

00:01:10.632 --> 00:01:14.340
As telemetry volume grows, detection engineers will need reliable pipelines,

00:01:14.340 --> 00:01:18.160
clear schemas, useful enrichment, and sustainable storage decisions.

00:01:18.160 --> 00:01:21.650
Detection engineering is the discipline of designing, building, maintaining, measuring,

00:01:21.650 --> 00:01:24.009
documenting, and improving security detections.

00:01:24.009 --> 00:01:28.720
It transforms telemetry into actionable defensive visibility and relies on collaboration

00:01:28.720 --> 00:01:29.920
across security teams.

00:01:29.920 --> 00:01:34.700
Mature programs use lifecycle management, testing, tuning, documentation, metrics,

00:01:34.700 --> 00:01:37.965
and continuous improvement to maintain effective defensive capabilities.

00:01:37.965 --> 00:01:40.475
Detection engineering is not simply writing alerts.

00:01:40.475 --> 00:01:44.540
It is the engineering practice of creating reliable visibility into security-relevant

00:01:44.540 --> 00:01:45.000
activity.
